  "query_preview": "..\n\nScattered showers have spread across most of the area overnight as \nthe prefrontal moisture belt has arrived. 850-700 moisture advection \nis bringing PWATs over 1.7 inches already this morning with around 2 \ninches slated for this afternoon. Warm sector profiles with a wealth \nof moisture will lead to poor lapse rates through the day with \nminimal CAPE values (max values around 200 J/kg). There has been no \nlightning as of 06Z in the vicinity, but there are some more \nmoderate showers reach up to around 35kft so with the addition of up \nto a couple hundred J/kg of CAPE this morning and the low level jet \nflaring up to around 40 knots through the morning and into the \nafternoon, we could get a few thunderstorms. New SPC Day 1 continues \nthe former Day 2 outlook with Marginal Risk of severe storms \nclipping Lenawee and Monroe counties. This is the area that could \npossibly draw up the most instability ahead of the cold front later \nthis afternoon to go with the ample shear present already. Any \nstronger storm may produce gusty winds with the strong flow just off \nthe deck, and damaging wind would be the primary threat with any \nsevere storms. Heavy rainfall will also be a threat today with any \ntraining cells due to high moisture content and potential training \nalong the prefrontal axis. \n\nThe prefrontal trough will clear the area by this evening with the \ncold front following by morning. Won't see a big drop off in temps \nThursday (mid to upper 70s) as the thermal trough lags behind the \nfront and will arrive later in the day Thursday, but the dewpoint \ndrop off will make it feel more pleasant with lower humidity. The \nthermal trough then hangs around a couple days to close out the work \nweek with 850mb temps around 10C. High pressure at the surface and \nlow amplitude longwave ridge will lead to a quiet couple days. Next \nchance of showers comes late Saturday as the next cold front \napproaches. At this point both the ECMWF and GFS stall the front \nover northern MI with the bulk of the forcing holding to the north, \nso will keep it at a slight chance for now.",
